{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/945791-older-characters","id":945791,"title":"Older characters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-07T18:37:03-07:00","id":945791,"title":"Older characters","content":"One thing that's always struck me as odd is that in <i>Vampire</i>, the player characters are immortals, but that aspect of the game is so rarely explored because the default player characters are fairly recently dead. While this makes sense from an ease of play standpoint (the average player can easier get into the mindset of someone who died yesterday or even in 1989 than someone from the 1600s), I wanted to hear input from other players on the subject.<br /> <br /> Have you ever played a character Embraced at least 100 years ago, and if so how did you roleplay it? Do you have any tips for helpings players get into a much older character?<br /> <br /> (And yes, I know <i>Thousand Years of Night</i> will address some of this. That book isn't out yet, and I wanted to discuss it with everyone else here.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 08-07-2016, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T19:01:35-07:00","id":945812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/945791-older-characters#post945791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that's always struck me as odd is that in <i>Vampire</i>, the player characters are immortals, but that aspect of the game is so rarely explored because the default player characters are fairly recently dead.<br /> <br /> Do you have any tips for helpings players get into a much older character?<br /> <br /> (And yes, I know <i>Thousand Years of Night</i> will address some of this. That book isn't out yet, and I wanted to discuss it with everyone else here.)</div> </div> </div> </div>One might look to Ancient Mysteries for tips, too, as it is also covered there. I've only played such characters as a Storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T19:09:54-07:00","id":945816,"title":"","content":"I personally dislike playing supernaturally old characters, because I feel that I can't do their vastly different and alien perspective justice. One of reasons why I never could get into elves and similar things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T20:38:51-07:00","id":945893,"title":"","content":"I played a vampire who was embraced in 700 Prague. Spent various centuries here and there in torpor and moving around the world a shit ton. He was in torpor from 1850 to 2015 and I had a blast walking him through waking up and seeing all these strange changes in the world. He loved elevators and escalators and this first time on a train was hilarious. He stole a cop car when he didn't know how to drive... Promptly crashed it. It was delightful.<br /> <br /> However he is very distant and closed off. He feels very alone as everyone he knew, human and kindred alike, has grown old and died ( or been killed ). He is often reckless because he is so very old, he feels he has lived his life. Nothing worse can happen than what already has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-07-2016, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T19:56:47-07:00","id":946692,"title":"","content":"One of my NPCs I made once was a Daeva elder with precognitive abilities who was embraced sometime during the Civil war, but had seen enough of the future to decide that she would fit in better in the 1980s, so she went to sleep until she could live out her neon dreams.... but she overslept and just woke up a couple years ago. She thus acts like a child of the 80s, which keeps her political rivals from realizing how old and powerful she really is. I imagine elders with precognitive abilities do stuff like that a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T01:39:29-07:00","id":946811,"title":"","content":"I've wondered about the extent to which this is an issue in Requiem 2e. I mean, we're told repeatedly that Kindred personalities can radically change; coming out of torpor, they're primed to alter themselves to fit into present-day society. To me that suggests a thousand year old vampire may not have all that different a mindset to a neonate, they just have these memories that perhaps don't fit all that well with their modern personality.<br /> <br /> It suggests to me that the problem with immortality in 2e isn't becoming stagnant, it's loosing your identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T05:39:21-07:00","id":946888,"title":"","content":"They're prepared for technological and societal changes, but an Aztec blood priest is still an Aztec blood priest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T06:15:58-07:00","id":946903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/945791-older-characters?p=946888#post946888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're prepared for technological and societal changes, but an Aztec blood priest is still an Aztec blood priest.</div> </div> </div> </div>An aztec priest is a social role with an associated belief system. If our vampire wakes from torpor and rapidly assimilates a modern perspective then they're not going to be that Aztec priest anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T06:39:07-07:00","id":946914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/945791-older-characters?p=946903#post946903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An aztec priest is a social role with an associated belief system. If our vampire wakes from torpor and rapidly assimilates a modern perspective then they're not going to be that Aztec priest anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>They'll appreciate civilization as they knew it has changed, but it wouldn't stops a priest from finding a new flock. If they're a true believer, they can just pick up where they left off. If they're a charlatan, they can just use modern cult techniques.<br /> <br /> Just because your civilization is gone doesn't mean that the blood god is, or that the modern world has no need for a blood priest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T08:29:09-07:00","id":946959,"title":"","content":"I think playing an older character is a great experiment. Part of the fun of being a Storyteller is that I can get into the heads of people who last breathed 50, 500, even a couple thousand years ago. How to play such a character? For my character who was Embraced around 1800, I worked out his backstory -- What was his environment like at the time, who were his family, and such (some basic research, nothing fancy). From there, I determined his personality and what was important to him. I thought about how outliving everything he knew might shape him. Then, into the ground he went until waking in modern times. Reestablishing himself in the modern world is where the fun comes in. I tend to think he is more mentally flexible than I would be, because that is a survival mechanism and the thing inside him is all about survival. The character may realize that what is is different than what he remembers, but knows instinctively that blending in is paramount. Therefore, he may actively refrain from doing the formerly &quot;done thing&quot;. You may wish to play it differently. Leopold in &quot;Kate and Leopold&quot; stands out and it is quite amusing, but a lone vampire who follows antiquated etiquette like that is liable to attract the wrong kind of notice -- and that could be what your story is about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}